  "claim": "Narcissa was criticised for being publicly tolerated as a singer due to her wealth, despite a lack of talent, like Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller. Sentence: Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller (April 14, 1876–1952), born Tryphosa Duncan Bates, was an American socialite, club woman and concert singer.\nPage: Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller. Sentence: She is often mentioned in the same context as Florence Foster Jenkins: both are apt to be criticised as people who were publicly tolerated and even celebrated as singers due to their wealth and social position, despite a lack of talent.\nPage: Florence Foster Jenkins. Sentence: Florence Foster Jenkins (born Narcissa Florence Foster; July 19, 1868 – November 26, 1944) was an American socialite and amateur soprano who was known and mocked for her flamboyant performance costumes and notably poor singing ability.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller. Sentence: Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller (April 14, 1876–1952), born Tryphosa Duncan Bates, was an American socialite, club woman and concert singer.\nPage: Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller. Sentence: She is often mentioned in the same context as Florence Foster Jenkins: both are apt to be criticised as people who were publicly tolerated and even celebrated as singers due to their wealth and social position, despite a lack of talent.\nPage: Florence Foster Jenkins. Sentence: Florence Foster Jenkins (born Narcissa Florence Foster; July 19, 1868 – November 26, 1944) was an American socialite and amateur soprano who was known and mocked for her flamboyant performance costumes and notably poor singing ability.",
