        "original_id": "be4544d4-9b38-5bae-9f30-e370095ee580",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller, Florence Foster Jenkins\n- Roles: socialite, club woman, concert singer, amateur soprano\n- Concepts: public criticism of untalented singers, wealth and social status\n\nFacts:\n- Florence Foster Jenkins was born Narcissa Florence Foster on July 19, 1868, and she became an American socialite and amateur soprano.\n- Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller was born Tryphosa Duncan Bates on April 14, 1876, and she became an American socialite, club woman, and concert singer.\n- Florence Foster Jenkins was known and mocked for flamboyant performance costumes and notably poor singing ability.\n- Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller is often mentioned alongside Florence Foster Jenkins because both were criticized as singers who were publicly tolerated or celebrated due to wealth and social position despite perceived lack of talent.\n- Florence Foster Jenkins died on November 26, 1944.\n- Tryphosa Bates-Batcheller died in 1952.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
